36
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:14,064
I keep hearing about images vs containers.

37
00:02:14,064 --> 00:02:15,781
What is it, really?

38
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:18,719
An image is a read-only template:

39
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:24,214
a file system plus metadata (which command to run, which user, which ports).

40
00:02:24,214 --> 00:02:27,034
A container is an instance of an image:

41
00:02:27,034 --> 00:02:33,903
the image's layers, plus a thin writable layer of its own, plus a running (or stopped) process.

42
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:38,169
One image can be the template for any number of containers,

43
00:02:38,169 --> 00:02:42,073
and changes inside a container never change the image.

44
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:47,078
Create three containers from the same image.

45
