If not, remove it and reuse the name; if it is, choose another name.

159
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,713
Got it.

160
00:10:27,713 --> 00:10:30,464
What do I need to remember?

161
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:37,830
Every container has a unique ID and a unique name; commands accept either, or an ID prefix.

162
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:42,391
--name chooses the name; docker rename changes it.

163
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:45,647
Names stay taken by exited containers:

164
00:10:45,647 --> 00:10:48,933
remove the old container or pick another name.

165
00:10:50,667 --> 00:10:53,096
Can you show me running Nginx?

166
00:10:53,633 --> 00:10:56,734
So far our containers ran a command and exited.

167
00:10:56,734 --> 00:10:58,912
A server container keeps running:

168
00:10:58,912 --> 00:11:04,454
its main process (here the Nginx web server) waits for requests until it is stopped.

169
