198
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:15,358
I keep hearing about port mapping.

199
00:13:15,358 --> 00:13:17,048
What is it, really?

200
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:21,339
-p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT publishes a container's port:

201
00:13:21,339 --> 00:13:28,816
Docker listens on HOST_PORT of your computer and forwards every connection to CONTAINER_PORT inside the container.

202
00:13:28,816 --> 00:13:37,671
The two numbers are independent, so ten Nginx containers can all listen on port 80 inside while each one gets a different port outside.

203
00:13:37,671 --> 00:13:41,934
