275
00:19:06,913 --> 00:19:09,665
What do I need to remember?

276
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:16,929
docker logs shows what the main process wrote to stdout and stderr, even after it exited.

277
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:21,951
--tail, -t, --since and -f narrow and follow the log.

278
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:27,954
Logs written to files inside the container are invisible to Docker:

279
00:19:27,954 --> 00:19:31,779
log to stdout, or link the file to /dev/stdout.

280
00:19:33,533 --> 00:19:37,953
What should I know about running commands in containers (exec)?

281
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:42,982
docker exec starts an additional process inside a running container:

282
00:19:42,982 --> 00:19:47,135
it shares the container's file system, network and environment.

283
00:19:47,135 --> 00:19:49,376
It is the tool for looking inside:

284
00:19:49,376 --> 00:19:53,265
read a configuration file, check what the application sees,

285
00:19:53,265 --> 00:19:58,736
test a connection from the container's point of view, or open an interactive shell.

286
00:19:58,736 --> 00:20:01,834
It does not restart or change the main process,

287
00:20:01,834 --> 00:20:06,514
and whatever you change by hand is lost when the container is replaced.

