315
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:03,399
Can you show me inspecting containers?

316
00:22:03,933 --> 00:22:09,285
docker inspect prints everything Docker knows about a container as JSON:

317
00:22:09,285 --> 00:22:12,779
its configuration (image, command, environment,

318
00:22:12,779 --> 00:22:15,901
ports, mounts), its state (running or not,

319
00:22:15,901 --> 00:22:22,889
exit code, start and finish times, whether it was killed for memory) and its network settings.

320
00:22:22,889 --> 00:22:29,133
It is the most precise answer to "what is this container, and what happened to it?".

321
00:22:29,133 --> 00:22:32,478
--format extracts exactly the field you need.

